@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@identificacion = 001-1234567-8

### Estado del servicio
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 1. Iniciar sesion
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "usuario": "banco.demo",
  "password": "Banco123*"
}

### 2. Crear API token con el JWT de sesion
# @name crearApiToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/api-token
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokenSesion}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Consultar historial completo en JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/{{identificacion}}/historial-crediticio
Authorization: Bearer {{crearApiToken.response.body.$.apiToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Consultar historial completo en XML
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/{{identificacion}}/historial-crediticio?format=xml
Authorization: Bearer {{crearApiToken.response.body.$.apiToken}}
Accept: application/xml

### 5. Consultar score crediticio
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/{{identificacion}}/score
Authorization: Bearer {{crearApiToken.response.body.$.apiToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Consultar endeudamiento
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/{{identificacion}}/endeudamiento
Authorization: Bearer {{crearApiToken.response.body.$.apiToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 7. Consultar ciudadano sin historial
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/003-1111111-2/historial-crediticio
Authorization: Bearer {{crearApiToken.response.body.$.apiToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Comprobar que el JWT del login no permite consultas (debe responder 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/{{identificacion}}/score
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.tokenSesion}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Comprobar una identificacion incorrecta (debe responder 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ciudadanos/123/score
Authorization: Bearer {{crearApiToken.response.body.$.apiToken}}
Accept: application/json
